{"id":"C2.2","doc":"C","title":"Pin Overview","words":1404,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The ESP32-S3 chip integrates multiple peripherals that require communication with the outside world."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"To keep the chip package size reasonably small, the number of available pins has to be limited."}]},{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"So the only way to route all the incoming and outgoing signals is through pin multiplexing."}]},{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Pin muxing is controlled via software programmable registers (see "},{"t":"link","href":"https://espressif.com/documentation/esp32-s3_technical_reference_manual_en.pdf#iomuxgpio-reg-summ","c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3 Technical Reference Manual"}]},{"t":"text","v":" > Chapter "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX and GPIO Matrix"}]},{"t":"text","v":")."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"All in all, the ESP32-S3 chip has the following types of pins:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO pins"}]},{"t":"text","v":" with the following predefined sets of functions to choose from:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Each IO pin has predefined "},{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX functions"}]},{"t":"text","v":" - see Table 2-4 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX Functions"}]}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Some IO pins have predefined "},{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"RTC functions"}]},{"t":"text","v":" - see Table 2-6 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"RTC Functions"}]}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Some IO pins have predefined "},{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"analog functions"}]},{"t":"text","v":" - see Table 2-8 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Analog Functions"}]}]}]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Predefined functions"}]},{"t":"text","v":" means that each IO pin has a set of direct connections to certain on-chip peripherals."}]},{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"During run-time, the user can configure which peripheral from a predefined set to connect to a certain pin at a certain time via memory mapped registers (see "},{"t":"link","href":"https://espressif.com/documentation/esp32-s3_technical_reference_manual_en.pdf#iomuxgpio","c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3 Technical Reference Manual"}]},{"t":"text","v":" > Chapter "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX and GPIO pins"}]},{"t":"text","v":")."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":12,"c":[{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Analog pins"}]},{"t":"text","v":" that have exclusively-dedicated analog functions - see Table 2-10 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Analog Pins"}]}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":13,"c":[{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Power pins"}]},{"t":"text","v":" that supply power to the chip components and non-power pins - see Table 2-11 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Power Pins"}]}]}]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":14,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Table 2-1 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Pin Overview"}]},{"t":"text","v":" gives an overview of all the pins."}]},{"n":15,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For more information, see the respective sections for each pin type below, or "},{"t":"xref","id":"C8","c":[{"t":"text","v":"C8 Consolidated Pin Overview"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 2-1. Pin Overview","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Pin No."}],[{"t":"text","v":"Pin Name"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Pin Type"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Pin Providing Power [2-5]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"At Reset [6]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"After Reset [6]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX [1]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"RTC IO MUX"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Analog"}]],"rows":[{"n":16,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"1"}],[{"t":"field","v":"LNA_IN"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Analog"}],[],[],[],[],[],[]]},{"n":17,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"2"}],[{"t":"text","v":"VDD3P3"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Power"}],[],[],[],[],[],[]]},{"n":18,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"3"}],[{"t":"text","v":"VDD3P